course: dictionary
lesson: 369
title: Learning from word parts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some long words are built from smaller parts you may already know. Look for a part you recognise, because it can give you a clue. Antimacassar starts with anti, which means against.
explain: An antimacassar is a small cloth, often lacy, put over the back or arms of a chair or sofa to keep it clean. Long ago, men put a hair oil called Macassar oil on their hair, and it stained the chairs. So the cloth was against the oil, and that is where the name comes from.
explain: Check your guess in the sentence. «She keeps a canary, several piebald mice and a restless revolving squirrel; at night the canary's cage is covered with an antimacassar (a cloth for the back of a chair).» The bracket gives the meaning, and a cloth fits the sentence, so your guess can be trusted.
fact: The word part anti means against, as in antisocial.
fact: «Antimacassar» means a small cloth, often lacy, put over the back or arms of a chair or sofa.
fact: Antimacassars were common in Victorian and Edwardian homes, so you will meet them in history lessons and old books.
fact: Some trains and planes still have antimacassars on their headrests.
exercise: «The old armchair had a lacy antimacassar on its back.» What is the antimacassar? | A lamp that gives out light | *A small cloth on the back of a chair | A small wooden box | A kind of cake
exercise: The word antimacassar starts with anti. What does anti mean? | Inside | Together | Very large | *Against
exercise: Why did people use an antimacassar long ago? | *To keep the chair clean from hair oil | To make the sofa softer to sit on | To make the chair warmer | To keep birds in a cage
test: In old books and history lessons, antimacassars show what kind of room? | A deep sea cave | *An old-fashioned, tidy parlour | A space rocket | A modern gym
test: What is the best way to check a guess about a new word? | Skip the whole text | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Ignore the sentence and guess again | Look only at the first letter
exam: Which meaning fits antimacassar in «She put an antimacassar on the armchair»? | A car part | A kind of hat | A small cake | *A small cloth on the back of a chair
